  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed as a suru verb ({哀願|あいがん}する) or as a noun modifier. Carries a strong emotional nuance — the person is desperately begging. Common in literary and dramatic contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {哀願|あいがん}する (to plead, to implore)\n- {哀願|あいがん}の{目|め} (pleading eyes)\n- {哀願|あいがん}の{声|こえ} (pleading voice)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {懇願|こんがん}: earnest entreaty — similar intensity, slightly more formal\n- {嘆願|たんがん}: petition, appeal — more formal, often used for official requests",
